DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/truisms-fiction-and-women-wri
 ting-a-lunch-workshop-with-author-marie-darrieussecq\n\nThe French and Ita
 lian Department and French Speaking Worlds: Here and Now invite you to a l
 unch workshop entitled “Truisms\, Fiction and Women’s writing” with 
 acclaimed author Marie Darrieussecq. Darrieussecq is a French novelist\, t
 ranslator\, and former psychoanalyst. She earned her doctorate in French l
 iterature in 1997 at the École Normale Supérieure. Her 1996 debut novel\
 , Truismes (Pig Tales\, trans. 1997)\, tells the story of a woman who slow
 ly turns into a pig amidst a tense and depraved political climate. It beca
 me one of the best-selling novels in France and was heralded by critics as
  a provocative social satire and multi-layered tale of feminist emancipati
 on. She has since published over 20 works spanning from novels\, children
 ’s books\, essays and biographies. Her novel Il faut beaucoup aimer les 
 hommes won the Prix Medicis in 2013 and her more recent works include Pas 
 dormir (Sleepless\, trans. 2021) and Fabriquer une femme (How to make a wo
 man\, trans. 2026). Darrieussecq’s rich oeuvre probes the unspoken bound
 aries of language and represents a fearless expression of the female body.
  All are welcome! \n\nRSVP for the lunch workshop here.
